"""Ellipses and the punctuation of an unfinished list.

Recognize ASCII, Unicode and TeX dots, numeric ranges, and code omissions.
Numbers and arithmetic/list separators strengthen inline ellipses. A whole
line of just three dots is a stronger omission marker. Spaced dots build
to the third dot, then fade into a dotted leader. The next list separator
can retain their strength. Other tokens are mostly zero.
